% expect-output: 6.0
% expect-output: 0.0
% expect-output: 112.0
% expect-output: 100.0
% Scenario: setcharwidth under a scale. The glyph procedure doubles the
% coordinate system, declares width 300 0 there, sets its own gray, and
% fills: the glyph's width in glyph space is 600 with no box (the glyph
% is not colour-independent), and at size 10 each glyph advances 6.
% Expect: 6.0 0.0, then 112.0 100.0.
/r { 1000 mul round 1000 div } def
/Bar 7 dict dup begin
  /FontType 3 def
  /FontMatrix [0.001 0 0 0.001 0 0] def
  /Encoding StandardEncoding def
  /FontBBox [0 0 600 800] def
  /BuildGlyph {
    pop pop
    2 2 scale
    300 0 setcharwidth
    0.5 setgray
    0 0 moveto 250 0 lineto 250 400 lineto closepath fill
  } def
end definefont pop
/Bar findfont 10 scalefont setfont
(a) stringwidth r exch r = =
100 100 moveto (aa) show currentpoint r exch r = =
showpage
